<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea Shipping - Steel scrap cargoes - July 10.</title>
<headline>S.Korea Shipping - Steel scrap cargoes - July 10.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the arrival schedule for major steel scrap vessels unloading at South Korean ports of Inchon, Pusan, Masan, Pohang, Kwangyang and Asan, as detailed on Thursday by South Korean surveyors.</p>
<p>-- INCHON PORT</p>
<p> VESSEL	    TONNE    ETA	  ETD	  BUYER</p>
<p> Canavera	  40,000   Mid-July		  Inchon</p>
<p> Feng Shou	 50,000   Mid-July		  Inchon</p>
<p> Rova		38,391   July 29		   Inchon</p>
<p>-- PUSAN PORT</p>
<p>No vessel calling schedule yet  </p>
<p>-- MASAN PORT</p>
<p> Yunling	   22,793   July 1     July 12    KISCO</p>
<p>-- POHANG PORT</p>
<p> Fivi		26,110   June 27    July 10    Kangwon</p>
<p> Delta Peace     48,000   July 4     July 31    Kangwon</p>
<p> Qupa		22,500   July 8     July 28    POSCO</p>
<p> Caspian-Trident 38,000   July 27		   POSCO</p>
<p> Seabee1	   42,000   July 27		   POSCO</p>
<p>-- KWANGYANG PORT</p>
<p> Faethon	   30,000   July 1     July 10    POSCO</p>
<p> Kupa		22,000   July 10		   POSCO</p>
<p> Feng Yao	  50,000   July 10		   POSCO</p>
<p> Al Qawiyyu	30,000   July 16		   POSCO</p>
<p> Lok Kranti	31,000   July 24		   POSCO</p>
<p> Xing Su Hai     30,000   Aug  2		    POSCO</p>
<p>-- ASAN PORT</p>
<p> Jade Orient     30,000   July 9		    Hanbo</p>
<p> Thornhill	 28,433   July 13		   Hanbo</p>
